 "answer": "To cap the number of concurrent API calls during a `promptfoo eval` run, you can use the `-j` or `--max-concurrency` option followed by the desired number of concurrent API calls. This option is available for several `promptfoo` commands, including `promptfoo eval`, `promptfoo redteam run`, and `promptfoo retry <evalId>`.\n\nFor example, to set the maximum number of concurrent API calls to 2 during a `promptfoo eval` run, you would use the following command:\n\n```bash\npromptfoo eval -j 2\n```\n\nAlternatively, using the full option name:\n\n```bash\npromptfoo eval --max-concurrency 2\n```\n\nThis setting limits the number of concurrent API calls to the specified number, helping manage resource usage and potentially improving performance depending on your infrastructure and use case.",
